      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "2015 BMJ Publishing Group Ltd.",
        "AbstractText": "We present a case of a 45-year-old woman with a right proximal tibiofibular dislocation she sustained after a fall during roller skating. Anteroposterior and lateral radiographs confirmed the diagnosis; there were no other injuries. The dislocation was reduced by direct manipulation after intra-articular infiltration, in our emergency department. The patient was treated with a long, non-weight bearing leg cast for 1\u2005week. After 4\u2005weeks, she had no pain and a full range of motion of the knee."
      },
